SPECIFICATION:

I would like you to implement a module named TopModule with the following
interface. All input and output ports are one bit unless otherwise
specified.

 - input  clk
 - input  areset
 - input  x
 - output z

The module should implement the following Mealy finite-state machine
which is an implementation of the 2's complementer. Implement using a
one-hot encoding. Resets into state A and reset is asynchronous
active-high.

  A --x=0 (z=0)--> A
  A --x=1 (z=1)--> B
  B --x=0 (z=1)--> B
  B --x=1 (z=0)--> B

Assume all sequential logic is triggered on the positive edge of the
clock.



CANDIDATE RTL TO ATTACK:
```verilog
module TopModule (
    input  wire clk,
    input  wire areset,
    input  wire x,
    output wire z
);

    // One-hot encoding: 2 states (A and B)
    // State A: 2'b01
    // State B: 2'b10
    reg [1:0] state_reg, state_next;

    localparam STATE_A = 2'b01;
    localparam STATE_B = 2'b10;

    // Asynchronous active-high reset
    always @(posedge clk or posedge areset) begin
        if (areset) begin
            state_reg <= STATE_A;
        end else begin
            state_reg <= state_next;
        end
    end

    // Next-state logic (Combinational)
    always @* begin
        state_next = state_reg; // default
        case (state_reg)
            STATE_A: begin
                if (x)
                    state_next = STATE_B;
                else
                    state_next = STATE_A;
            end
            STATE_B: begin
                state_next = STATE_B;
            end
            default: begin
                state_next = STATE_A;
            end
        endcase
    end

    // Output logic (Mealy: depends on current state and input x)
    assign z = (state_reg == STATE_A && x == 1'b1) || 
               (state_reg == STATE_B && x == 1'b0);

endmodule
```

